  "reasoning_content": "We need answer user: \"Write a detailed tutorial on implementing a bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include a complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, and include tests. Continue with a worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and use meaningful prose and code.\"\n\nNeed produce final answer detailed tutorial. Need include complete class, get/put behavior, edge cases, tests, worked example, complexity. Use Python code. Need be precise.\n\nLet's plan.\n\nTopic: bounded LRU cache using collections.OrderedDict.\n\nWe can implement class LRUCache:\n- __init__(self, capacity: int): if capacity <=0? Edge case. Could raise ValueError or handle no storage. Need discuss. For bounded LRU, capacity positive. If capacity 0, no items can be stored; get returns None, put discards. We can choose to raise ValueError for capacity < 0 and allow 0? Better precise: if capacity < 0 raise ValueError; if capacity == 0, cache stores nothing. Or require positive. Let's implement robust: if capacity < 0: raise ValueError; self._capacity = capacity; self._cache = OrderedDict()\n- get(key, default=None): if key in cache: move_to_end(key); return cache[key]; else return default.\n- put(key, value): if key in cache: move_to_end(key); cache[key]=value (or update then move? OrderedDict.__setitem__ on existing key does not change order? Need check: In Python OrderedDict, updating existing key does not change order. So need move_to_end after update or before. If key in cache: self._cache[key]=value; self._cache.move_to_end(key). else: if len == capacity: popitem(last=False) (remove oldest); if capacity >0: self._cache[key]=value. If capacity ==0: do nothing.\n- maybe __len__, __contains__, peek? Could include.\n- Need explain OrderedDict: maintains insertion order; move_to_end(key, last=True) moves to end (most recent); popitem(last=False) removes first (least recently used). In Python 3.3+? OrderedDict supports move_to_end, popitem(last=False). We can mention.\n\nNeed tests. Use unittest or pytest. Include tests:\n- test_get_missing returns default\n- test_put_and_get\n- test_update_existing_key moves to MRU\n- test_evicts_least_recent",
